<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2">
  <Document>
    <name>🧊 LIVE ICE THICKNESS</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<p><b>Time fetched:</b> 4:50PM EDT</p><h2>LIVE ICE THICKNESS</h2><p><b>Gradient key</b><br><img src="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/ice_thickness/legend.png" width="600" alt="gradient key"><br>Ice thickness (inches, WMO stage-derived estimates): thinner <b>0 in</b> (light blue) → blue → deep blue → thicker <b>12 in</b> (purple). No color is painted where there is no ice; fainter = partial concentration.</p><p>This entry auto-refreshes from the live overlay (source: U.S. National Ice Center (NAIS) daily Great Lakes ice analysis, SIGRID-3 shapefile).</p><p>Turn on/off independently of the other ice, wave and temperature layers. Add this file once; new source cycles appear automatically.</p><p><i>Not endorsed by NOAA.</i></p>]]></description>
    <NetworkLink>
      <name>🧊 LIVE ICE THICKNESS — auto-refresh</name>
      <Link>
        <href>https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/kml/live/Great_Lakes_Live_Ice_Thickness.kml</href>
        <refreshMode>onInterval</refreshMode>
        <refreshInterval>21600</refreshInterval>
      </Link>
    </NetworkLink>
  </Document>
</kml>
